      "id": "vP1BbqZ_dnM",
      "title": "Is Betelgeuse About to Explode?"
    },
    "spoken": "Betelgeuse, normally one of the brightest stars in the sky, began to fade. By February 2020, it had dropped to about a third of its usual brightness. Was Betelgeuse about to explode? A huge bubble of gas had burst out from the star's surface and drifted away. As it cooled, it turned into a cloud of dust, and the dust blocked part of the star from our view.",
